      "end_seconds": 3.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "evening. Long day, I imagine. Sit down"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.97,
      "end_seconds": 6.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Hi doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 7.72,
      "end_seconds": 12.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.74,
      "end_seconds": 20.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.57,
      "text": "that's fine sit down we'll go through it it together so what's been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 21.51,
      "end_seconds": 29.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "it's been feeling dizzy when I stand, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.61,
      "end_seconds": 42.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.68,
      "end_seconds": 49.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "I notice it more with standing up quickly. Pretty severe, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.74,
      "end_seconds": 56.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 56.42,
      "end_seconds": 62.37,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in doctor quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.06,
      "end_seconds": 65.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Later thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.51,
      "end_seconds": 77.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "I've also had muscle cramps, for about two weeks with muscle cramps, about a seven out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.11,
      "end_seconds": 81.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "has there been dark urine too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.32,
      "end_seconds": 84.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Yes, since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.31,
      "end_seconds": 90.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "any chest pain, blood in the stool or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.03,
      "end_seconds": 108.58,
      "duration_seconds": 16.55,
      "text": "No uh no chest pain no blood in the stool no fever. I did have a very dry mouth at one point but that that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.24,
      "end_seconds": 112.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Any fainting, confusion or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.49,
      "end_seconds": 116.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, no fainting, confusion or vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.54,
      "end_seconds": 121.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.0,
      "end_seconds": 126.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "um, bowels are regular, nothing odd"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.9,
      "end_seconds": 133.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "What about allergies to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.06,
      "end_seconds": 144.01,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once years ago. I don't remember which one or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.7,
      "end_seconds": 162.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "any diagnoses you've been given before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.05,
      "end_seconds": 173.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.73,
      "text": "yes, diabetes i've had high blood pressure for about ten years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.12,
      "end_seconds": 185.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.19,
      "text": "yes, diabetes and high blood pressure are known to us, good to have that clear a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.32,
      "end_seconds": 199.09,
      "duration_seconds": 12.77,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day. I walk for about half an hour most days. Yes, I live on my own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.59,
      "end_seconds": 213.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 215.19,
      "end_seconds": 230.24,
      "duration_seconds": 15.05,
      "text": "Well, he is on metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day, I give it to him. He is on ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.05,
      "end_seconds": 237.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "I used to take glimepiride, but I stopped it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 237.73,
      "end_seconds": 247.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.8 degrees, pulse is 99 beats a minute, saturation 97 percent, pressure 98 over 65."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.38,
      "end_seconds": 249.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "okay noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.67,
      "end_seconds": 253.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "let me examine it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.95,
      "end_seconds": 257.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "let me look at this properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.33,
      "end_seconds": 271.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.17,
      "text": "Your mouth is quite dry and the skin is a little slow to spring back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.98,
      "end_seconds": 307.12,
      "duration_seconds": 32.14,
      "text": "good, that's the examination so, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is dehydration from a stomach bug i can't rule out an electrolyte imbalance yet i'm gonna order blood salts, for dehydration i'm going to order a kidney function test, for dehydration for this, ORS, 1 sachet, after each loose motion, for two days that should help with dehydration"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.57,
      "end_seconds": 335.23,
      "duration_seconds": 24.66,
      "text": "Small frequent sips are better than a big glass at once and keep going even if you don't feel thirsty. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids two to three litres a day if you can and get proper rest. Let's plan a check next week. Alright I'll see you out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.06,
      "end_seconds": 339.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "All good here. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.41,
      "end_seconds": 341.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Bye for now."
    }
  ]
